 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Landing Page SEO Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is landing page SEO?\", \"a\": \"Landing page SEO is the work of creating a landing page and optimizing it to rank in search results, then turning its visitors into leads or sales. A Denver page for a moving company is one landing page for SEO: written to rank for Denver movers and to collect quote requests.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build an SEO landing page?\", \"a\": \"Build it around a single query. Put that query in the title tag and the H1, answer it in the opening section, then ask for the lead. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a> writes the page and its schema markup from one prompt, lead form included.\"},{\"q\": \"Do landing pages help SEO?\", \"a\": \"They can, when each page carries content of its own. When pages are near duplicates, Google picks one as canonical, and its results usually point to that page. For pages that only take paid clicks, build a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/ppc-landing-page'>PPC landing page</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the first steps in landing page SEO optimization?\", \"a\": \"Start with Search Console when the work is SEO for landing pages that already exist. Its Performance report lists the queries each page appears for, with clicks and impressions for every one. Where a query earns impressions but the page has no section that answers it, write that section next. On Emergent, that new section takes one chat message, not a redesign.\"}, {\"q\": \"What belongs on a landing page SEO checklist?\", \"a\": \"Close a landing page SEO checklist with two checks before launch and one after it. Run the schema through Google's Rich Results Test. Confirm the canonical tag points at the page's own URL. After publishing, use URL Inspection in Search Console to see whether Google can index the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a landing page SEO template?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as an outline, not a design: one set of sections reused across every city or feature page, with the copy written fresh for each. Google's spam policies list pages targeted at specific cities that funnel users to one page as doorway abuse. Emergent can build the set from one outline and a table of details per page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes good SEO landing page design?\", \"a\": \"On SEO landing pages, check two design choices against Google's guidance: image alt text and the phone layout. Google uses alt text, along with the page around it, to understand what an image shows. Describe each one plainly. Google also indexes the mobile version of a page, which means the phone layout needs the same content as the desktop one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are search engine landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Search engine landing pages are pages meant to be found through organic search, such as feature pages or city pages, unlike pages that only get ad or email traffic. Let Google index each of them. For A/B test variants, Google recommends a canonical tag pointing to the original, not noindex. Keep noindex for pages that should never rank, such as a thank you page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best landing page SEO tips?\", \"a\": \"Keep one page per query across the whole site. If Search Console shows two of your URLs trading places for the same query, merge them or retarget one. Put the query in a short URL slug, and write the first sentence of the page so it could stand alone as the answer.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good SEO landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/law-firm-landing-page'>law firm landing page</a> for estate planning in Tucson is a good model: it names the practice and the city in its H1 and places the consultation form after the answer. For your own query, study what the top pages show on the first screen. Each page Emergent builds is plain code you can export to your GitHub repository on paid plans.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
